---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/02-12/', brochure='https://industry.nikon.com/de-de/wp-content/uploads/sites/14/2026/02/eclipse-lv-n-en.pdf', official='https://industry.nikon.com/en-us/products/industrial-microscopy/industrial-microscopes/upright-eclipse-lv100nda-lv100nd/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Nikon LV100ND LED · reflected optical inspection" description="Measure a 40 μm grating from an inert synthetic reflectance image at two objectives and compare object-space field, scale, and focus." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment lv"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/02-12/">← Equipment 02-12</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#lv-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">02-12 · REFLECTED BRIGHTFIELD / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Nikon ECLIPSE LV100ND LED</h2><p>Inspect a synthetic engraved coupon in reflected brightfield. A 40 µm pitch spans twice as many pixels at 20× as it does at 10×, but its physical spacing stays the same.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Manual microscope</h3><div id="lv-view" aria-label="Orbitable LV100ND LED with binocular eyepieces, objective turret, stage, illumination controls and focus knobs"></div><div class="bar"><button data-lv-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-lv-view="stage">Objectives & stage</button><button data-lv-view="rear">Rear optics</button></div><p id="lv-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The cyan turret target switches objectives. The right focus knob returns focus to nominal zero. Sample motion in 3D is exaggerated.</p></section>
<section><h3>Virtual image plane</h3><canvas width="512" height="320" id="lv-image" aria-label="Generated reflected-light grayscale grating with an optional known mark and 20 micrometer scale bar"></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Objective<select id="lv-objective"><option value="10">10× / NA 0.30</option><option value="20">20× / NA 0.45</option></select></label><label>Focus (µm)<input id="lv-focusUm" type="number" min="-30" max="30" step="any" value="0"/></label><label>View center X (µm)<input id="lv-xUm" type="number" min="-90" max="90" step="any" value="0"/></label><label>View center Y (µm)<input id="lv-yUm" type="number" min="-90" max="90" step="any" value="0"/></label><label>Illumination factor<input id="lv-illumination" type="number" min=".05" max="1.4" step="any" value="1"/></label><label class="check"><input id="lv-mark" type="checkbox" checked/> Mark known artificial flaw</label></div>
<div class="bar"><button id="lv-capture" class="primary">Capture and measure</button><button id="lv-compare">Measure both objectives</button><button id="lv-focus">Set nominal focus</button><button id="lv-reset">Reset</button></div>
<p id="lv-status" aria-live="polite">Default coupon in focus; capture or compare both settings.</p><output id="lv-view-info"></output><output id="lv-comparison"></output>
<div class="bar"><button id="lv-png" disabled>Calibrated PNG</button><button id="lv-json" disabled>Image metadata JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="lv-evidence"><h3>Geometry and verification</h3><p>Selected configuration: manual LV100ND LED (not motorized LV100NDA LED), reflected brightfield illumination, 3 × 2 stage, manual turret, and CFI TU Plan Fluor EPI 10× MUE12100 and 20× MUE12200. <a href={official}>Nikon official product and configuration</a> distinguishes the variants. <a href={brochure+'#page=7'}>LV-N brochure, printed pp. 12–13</a> shows the exact objective specifications and orthogonal views. The visual stand follows the drawing configuration, and the digital scene uses an ideal virtual detector, not a specific Nikon camera.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="640" height="438" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original perspective rendering of the LV100ND LED body, angled eyepieces, objectives, and stage"/><figcaption>Original front render. Compared against the <a href="https://industry.nikon.com/en-us/wp-content/uploads/sites/13/2025/03/LV100ND-LED-2.jpg">Nikon LV100ND LED photograph</a> for the optical head, manual controls and stage arrangement.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="640" height="438" src={base+'side.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original side rendering of the C-shaped Nikon stand and rear illuminator"/><figcaption>Original side render. Nikon’s side elevation, printed p. 13, establishes the 386 mm base depth and overall extent. Unlisted component profiles and rear ports are inferred.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Specification / case</th><th>Reference</th><th>Actual / meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>LV100ND LED drawing</td><td>Base 251 mm wide × 386 mm deep; 506 mm high; 627 mm nominal overall depth</td><td>Nominal GLB anchors; exact optical accessory placement is not a mechanical drawing.</td></tr>
<tr><td>TU Plan Fluor EPI</td><td>10× NA 0.30, WD 17.5 mm; 20× NA 0.45, WD 4.5 mm</td><td>Documented manufacturer lens profiles in this model.</td></tr>
<tr><td>40 µm grating at 10×</td><td>80 px at 0.50 µm/px; width 256 µm</td><td>80 px, 40.000 µm; tolerated up to one image pixel.</td></tr>
<tr><td>40 µm grating at 20×</td><td>160 px at 0.25 µm/px; width 128 µm</td><td>160 px, 40.000 µm; tolerated up to one image pixel.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ideal Rayleigh at 550 nm</td><td>1.118 µm at 10×; 0.746 µm at 20×</td><td>Ideal formula, not a device accuracy or contrast calibration.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The synthetic target has a sinusoidal 40 µm grating and a 1.25 µm contrast strip. The ideal 512 × 320, 5 µm pixel image plane is projected via <code>sample spacing = detector pitch / objective magnification</code>. Pixel centers turn the stage center and object-space pitch into a physical X/Y position. <a href="https://www.microscopyu.com/microscopy-basics/modulation-transfer-function">Nikon’s circular-pupil MTF</a> supplies the ideal incoherent factor and diffraction cutoff. Pixel-aperture integration uses a sinc factor; focus adds a Gaussian approximation to the geometric defocus blur. An apparent fine-feature contrast loss is not a measured point spread function. The 40 µm pitch is estimated from median spacing of rising midlevel crossings in an 8-bit image row without using its known nominal value. The known synthetic flaw marker is not an automated detector.</p>
<p><a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={base+'lv100nd.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'reference-cases.json'}>Reference cases</a> · <a href={base+'example-metadata.json'}>Output format example</a> · <a href={base+'example-inspection.png'}>Example synthetic image</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No experimental data, hardware calibration, external sample import or headset use claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
